summary: "This working paper examines how firms respond to labor shocks. Using county-level variation from the rollout of the Secure Communities program, I study how farms adjust to increased labor insecurity. Preliminary evidence suggests that, rather than raising native wages or employment, farms respond to immigration enforcement–induced labor shortages by shifting crop mix and increasing mechanization."
